# Frontend Standards (Next.js + shadcn/ui)

## Stack

- **Next.js 16** (App Router, not Pages Router)
- **React 19**, **TypeScript** strict mode
- **shadcn/ui** + **Tailwind CSS v4**
- Backend API at `http://localhost:8000/api/v1` via `/api/*` rewrite
- Auth: `ht_session` cookie (email + password)

## UI/UX standards — enforced repo-wide

- **Primitives from `@f0rge/ui`** — Button, Card, Dialog, Input, Select, etc. Never copy shadcn components into `apps/`
- **shadcn CLI additions** land in `libs/ui`, never `apps/marrow/frontend/components/ui`
- **Icons:** lucide-react only
- **Toasts:** sonner only
- **Dark mode:** next-themes (via profile menu theme toggle)
- **Server state:** react-query (`@tanstack/react-query`) via hooks in `lib/api/hooks/`
- **Dates:** shared formatters from `@f0rge/ui` (`formatLocalDate`, `formatDisplayDate`)
- **API client:** `@f0rge/ui/api` — never re-implement `ApiError` / `handleResponse`
- **Loading/empty/error states:** use shared `FetchError` from `@f0rge/ui`
- **Shared lib components:** semantic tokens only (`var(--primary)`, `text-muted-foreground`) — apps own token values + `--marrow-*` brand vars

## Core Principles

- **Simplicity first** — readable over clever; duplicate beats wrong abstraction
- **~150 lines max per file** — split when longer
- Most pages are **client components** by design (react-query → FastAPI); keep `'use client'` off presentational leaves that don't need it
- Co-locate `page.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx` in route folders

## Component Architecture

- Single responsibility; explicit TypeScript prop interfaces
- Composition over configuration
- Use `@f0rge/ui` primitives — don't rebuild what exists in the shared lib
- Descriptive names: `IngredientTagEditor` not `Editor1`

## State & Data

- **URL state first** (searchParams for filters/pagination)
- API hooks in `apps/marrow/frontend/lib/api/hooks.ts`
- Local state (`useState`) only for UI (dropdowns, modals, inputs)
- Always handle loading, error, and empty states
- Export shared types from `types/`

## TypeScript & Styling

- Strict mode, **no `any`**
- Tailwind utilities directly; `cn()` for conditional classes
- Responsive, mobile-first (this is a mobile-first app)
- Semantic HTML; keyboard accessible; `aria-label` where needed

## Forms

Controlled components, inline validation errors, disable submit during submission, clear success/error feedback.

## Customize-Hub UX Contract (health-tracker)

Daily check-in (`/checkin/[date]`) is **data-entry only**. Structural changes live in `/customize`.

### Governance tiers

| Tier | Examples | User can | Where |
|------|----------|----------|-------|
| **Core** | Wellbeing, Gut, Bristol, Food | Show/hide sections only | `/customize/reorder`, `/customize/core-scales` |
| **Catalog** | Supplements, Diet tags | Pick from DB list | `/customize/catalogs` |
| **Custom** | Trackers, Symptoms | Full CRUD | `/customize/trackers`, `/customize/symptoms` |

### Input primitives (approved set only)

Segmented scale, 7-cell grid (Bristol), binary segmented, stepper, pill multi-select, severity row (0–10), free text (Notes).

### Daily-page visual contract

- No `+`, `…`, `Manage`, `Add`, `Edit`, or `Archive` on daily cards
- Card header: `LABEL` + `TierPill`; optional eye collapse toggle **mobile only** (`<lg`)
- Desktop (`lg+`): all visible sections always expanded; reduce clutter via Customize → Reorder & visibility
- Cards render in `cardOrder`, skipping `hiddenCards`
- Notes exempt (free text, can be hidden)

### Row anatomy (customize screens)

`[drag-handle 16px] [icon 32px] [name + meta flex-1] [actions ≤2]` — single `RowItem` at `components/customize/row-item.tsx`.

### Contract violations — stop and consult

Inline `+` on daily card, `…` overflow on card header, separate archived-items page, fourth tier, editable Core labels.

## Onboarding tour

Guided first-login tour uses **react-joyride v3** via `components/onboarding/`.

- Step definitions: `components/onboarding/tour-steps.ts` (single source of truth)
- Provider: `components/onboarding/onboarding-provider.tsx` (mounted in `providers.tsx`)
- Replay: Settings → Help → Replay app tour

**Keep in sync:** Any PR that changes bottom nav, check-in cards, customize hub, or primary empty-state pages must update tour steps and matching `data-tour` anchors.

## Quality Gate (before completing)

1. `npm run build` — must succeed
2. `npm run lint` — must pass
3. Verify render + edge cases (empty, loading, errors)
4. Test mobile viewport

## Decision Framework

1. Will a junior dev understand this in 6 months?
2. Am I solving a problem I don't have yet?
3. Can `@f0rge/ui` do this instead?
4. Should this state be in the URL?

## Commands

```bash
npm ci   # root workspaces install (from repo root)
npx nx run marrow-frontend:dev    # :3000
npx nx run-many -t lint typecheck build --projects f0rge-ui,marrow-frontend
```

For deep frontend work, delegate to the `frontend-dev` sub-agent in `~/.cursor/agents/`.
